          "path": "lib.distance_squared",
          "kind": "function",
          "private": false,
          "signature": "fn distance_squared(a: Point, b: Point): i32",
          "docs": "Returns the squared distance between two points.\n\nThis is cheaper than a distance because it needs no square root.\n\n# Errors\n\nIt never fails. [Circle.new] is the call that can, with [GeometryError.NegativeRadius].\n\n```\n# use geometry.{Point, distance_squared}\nlet d = distance_squared(Point.new(0, 0), Point.new(3, 4))\nassert_eq(d, 25)\n```",
